    "narrative": "As we move into the final stretch of the 2026 season, the offensive output for Ghost Ride the WHIP hinges on capitalizing on favorable matchups against vulnerable arms. Today\u2019s premier play is undoubtedly **Brice Turang**, who carries a solid 67.08 efficiency score into his matchup against the southpaw Ray. While we generally weigh the platoon disadvantage for **Brice Turang** against lefties, the opposing SP_xERA of 4.98 creates a high-ceiling environment that offsets the L/L split. Batting out of the #2 hole, he remains our highest-projected source of speed today\u2014a critical asset given our organizational mandate to chase the scarcest category in 5x5 Roto.\n\nOur bench decision-making process was relatively straightforward, though **Travis Bazzana** was the primary point of contention. **Travis Bazzana** posted a 29.84, falling well below our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" due to an inefficient matchup against Smith\u2019s 3.07 xERA. We are effectively preserving our game caps by sitting him, especially with heavy hitters like **Corbin Carroll**, **Josh Naylor**, and **James Wood** sidelined entirely by today\u2019s team off-days. We are currently navigating a thin depth chart; with **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Trevor Story**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Max Muncy**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Griffin Conine**, and **Edwin Arroyo** all monitoring the wire, we must remain disciplined with our remaining starts. Should the weather or late-scratches impact the confirmed lineups, we will pivot, but for now, we are comfortable letting **Travis Bazzana** rest while banking the efficiency of **Brice Turang**.",
